    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and adjusted duplicate detection with minimal structural impact \u2014 small, cohesive units, each with little surrounding complexity:\n\n**New file \u2014 `util/Soundex.java`**: a standalone American Soundex coder (`Soundex.of`), shared by both the util and controller packages. No surrounding class complexity to hold.\n\n**`util/IdentityKeys.of`**: now returns `SHA-256 hex(normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`. Added a private `sha256hex` helper. `isDuplicate` is unchanged \u2014 it still drives the 409, still filters out `deleted` owners; the blocklist stays applied first in the controller. The mapper already exposes this via `IdentityKeys.of`, so `identityKey` is now a 64-char hex string (satisfies `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`; identical identity \u2192 same key \u2192 409 for `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity`).\n\n**`PossibleDuplicates.matchId`**: the soft match now triggers when `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match but the whole `identityKey` differs \u2014 so same-name/same-postcode/different-telephone owners surface as soft matches instead of self-matching.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`**: removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block (2 lines). Duplicate detection is now solely the identity key. I left `Households.isDuplicate` in place (dead but harmless) rather than touch a second file, keeping the file-count multiplier and the big-controller WMC_other exposure to a minimum \u2014 only the one 2-line deletion inside that large class.\n\nNet: 3 tiny edits plus one small new class; the only change inside the large controller is a 2-line removal.",
